    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: fiscal-year basis for date-derived values\n\nThe fiscal year starts **1 July** and is labelled by the calendar year it *ends* in (Australian convention, matching the app's AU regions/timezones) \u2014 e.g. a registration date of `2026-09-05` (Jul\u2013Dec) falls in fiscal year 2027 \u2192 `FY27`.\n\n**`Owner.java`** (`model/`)\n- Added `Owner.fiscalYear(LocalDate)` \u2014 the single shared rule: `month \u2265 7 ? year+1 : year`.\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` \u2014 a `@Transient` derived read returning `\"FY<YY>\"` from the (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`, or `null` when absent. MapStruct auto-maps it onto the generated DTO by name, like the other derived getters.\n- `hasTenureBonus(...)` now counts **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYear(today) \u2212 fiscalYear(registration) > 1`) instead of a 365-day window, preserving the original \"over one year\" threshold.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `membershipYearSegment(...)` now derives its two-digit segment from `Owner.fiscalYear(registrationDate)`, so the membership identifier's year segment uses the fiscal year (e.g. `NSW-1A2B3C4D-M27`). It shares the one fiscal-year rule on `Owner` rather than duplicating it.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**\n- Added the read-only `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema (this is what generates `OwnerDto.getFiscalYear`/`setFiscalYear`), and updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to the fiscal-year semantics.\n\nThe stored `registrationDate` was already business-day-adjusted by `resolveRegistrationDate`, so all three values derive from that adjusted date. The audit log confirms end-to-end behaviour: `registrationDate=2026-09-07 ... membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27`.\n\nTest suite: **1 run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 the new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` acceptance test passes.",
